From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] mouse: Scroll Speed for the mouse and the touchpad

Scrolling distance could not be changed anywhere: libinput has no
option for it and GNOME never offered one. Luma's compositor now scales
scrolling per kind of device, and Mouse & Touchpad gets a Scroll Speed
slider in the Mouse section and in the touchpad's Scrolling section,
styled like Pointer Speed (Slow to Fast) with a reset button that is
available whenever the speed is not the default.

The slider runs over the base-2 logarithm of the stored multiple
(0.25 to 4.0), so Slow and Fast are equally far from the middle, and
the middle snaps to exactly 1.0, which the compositor treats as
unchanged. The settings, org.projectluma.peripherals.mouse and
.touchpad scroll-speed, come from Mutter; when they are not installed
the rows are hidden.
